sequenceDiagram
    autonumber

    actor Caller as 👤 Remote Caller (Cellular Line)
    participant Tower as 📡 Cell Tower (Jio / Airtel VoLTE)
    participant Modem as 📱 iQOO Z9 Baseband Modem<br/>(MT6878 / Dimensity 7200)
    participant DSP as 🎛️ MediaTek Audio DSP<br/>(Telephony Audio HAL)
    participant Telecom as ⚙️ Android Telecom / App<br/>(InCallService & CallManager)
    participant Pi_Bridge as 📻 Raspberry Pi Zero 2 W<br/>(BlueZ HFP-HF + PipeWire)
    participant Host_PC as 🖥️ Host Windows PC<br/>(ASR + Ollama 3B + TTS)

    Note over Caller,Host_PC: AI_CALL Phase 9.3 — Verified Bidirectional Cellular Audio Call Flow

    %% -------------------------------------------------------------
    %% 1. CALL ARRIVAL & BLUETOOTH SCO ROUTE SETUP
    %% -------------------------------------------------------------
    rect rgb(240, 245, 255)
    Note over Caller,Telecom: 1. Cellular Call Signaling & Hardware Audio Routing
    Caller->>Tower: Initiates phone call to user primary mobile number
    Tower->>Modem: Cellular VoLTE RF paging / call setup
    Modem->>Telecom: Telecom Framework alerts incoming call
    Telecom->>Telecom: InCallService answers call (call.answer(0))
    Telecom->>DSP: Sets call audio route: ROUTE_BLUETOOTH
    DSP->>DSP: Bypasses internal phone speaker & physical mic (AEC inactive)
    DSP->>Pi_Bridge: Establishes bidirectional Bluetooth eSCO link (16kHz mSBC)
    end

    %% -------------------------------------------------------------
    %% 2. DOWNLINK AUDIO PATH (CALLER TO AI)
    %% -------------------------------------------------------------
    rect rgb(240, 255, 245)
    Note over Caller,Host_PC: 2. Downlink Path: Caller Speech to Local AI Pipeline
    Caller->>Tower: Speaks English utterance into handset microphone
    Tower->>Modem: Transmits AMR-WB / EVS voice frames over VoLTE
    Modem->>DSP: Baseband decodes voice into 16kHz linear PCM
    DSP->>Pi_Bridge: Streams digital audio packets over Bluetooth eSCO Downlink
    Pi_Bridge->>Pi_Bridge: BlueZ 5.65+ receives SCO packets via HCI socket
    Pi_Bridge->>Pi_Bridge: PipeWire ALSA capture node (bluez_input.*) outputs raw 16kHz PCM
    Pi_Bridge->>Host_PC: Streams PCM over USB OTG Cable (CDC-NCM Ethernet Gadget, <1ms)
    end

    %% -------------------------------------------------------------
    %% 3. LOCAL AI PROCESSING PIPELINE (100% OFFLINE & ENGLISH-ONLY)
    %% -------------------------------------------------------------
    rect rgb(245, 245, 255)
    Note over Host_PC: 3. Host PC Voice Engine Execution (Zero Cloud Dependency):<br/>• English ASR (SAPI 8.0 / faster-whisper base.en): ~300ms<br/>• Deterministic Language Guardrail (Strict English): <1ms<br/>• Local Reasoning (Ollama qwen2.5:3b CPU): ~1,200ms<br/>• English Speech Synthesis (Windows SAPI5 David WAV): ~130ms
    end

    %% -------------------------------------------------------------
    %% 4. UPLINK AUDIO PATH (AI TO CALLER)
    %% -------------------------------------------------------------
    rect rgb(255, 245, 240)
    Note over Host_PC,Caller: 4. Uplink Path: AI Speech Injected into Cellular Uplink
    Host_PC->>Pi_Bridge: Returns synthesized 16kHz PCM speech buffer via USB (<1ms)
    Pi_Bridge->>Pi_Bridge: Injects PCM into PipeWire ALSA playback node (bluez_output.*)
    Pi_Bridge->>Pi_Bridge: PipeWire mSBC software encoder compresses into 60-byte SCO frames
    Pi_Bridge->>DSP: Transmits mSBC packets over Bluetooth eSCO Microphone Uplink
    DSP->>Modem: Routes Bluetooth mic stream directly to Baseband Transmit Buffer (TX)
    Modem->>Tower: Modulates AMR-WB speech over VoLTE RF cellular uplink
    Tower->>Caller: Delivers audio to remote caller phone
    Caller->>Caller: 🔊 Remote Caller hears natural, clear English AI agent voice!
    end

    %% -------------------------------------------------------------
    %% 5. HUMAN TAKEOVER & SAFETY GUARDRAILS
    %% -------------------------------------------------------------
    rect rgb(255, 250, 235)
    Note over Caller,Telecom: 5. Deterministic Human Takeover & Disconnect Safety
    opt User Taps "Take Over" on Phone UI
        Telecom->>DSP: Audio route instantly switched from ROUTE_BLUETOOTH to ROUTE_EARPIECE
        DSP->>Pi_Bridge: Tears down eSCO audio channel
        Caller->>Modem: Caller voice immediately heard in user ear; user speaks normally.
    end
    opt Bluetooth Disconnects or Bridge Loses Power
        DSP->>DSP: Hardware SCO timeout detected (<50ms)
        DSP->>Telecom: Auto-reverts route to internal earpiece; call remains connected.
    end
    end
